{"team":"GB","col":"#FFD84D","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":59.6,"adot":8.8,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Built to Run</h2><p>Run identity is the through-line here: GB call pass on <strong>-6%</strong> of snaps relative to what the situation expects (league -2%), and when they get ahead they lean even harder on the ground \u2014 just 36% pass on early downs with a lead. This is a ball-control operation built to shorten games.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>They spread the ball as much as anyone \u2014 the WR1 commands only <strong>18%</strong> of targets (league ~23%). Volume is democratic here, which suppresses any single receiver's ceiling but props up the TE and secondary options.</p><p>They push it downfield \u2014 average depth of target <strong>8.8 yards</strong> with 23% of throws traveling 15+, a vertical passing game that trades completions for boom-or-bust yardage.</p><p>By the numbers it's an efficient unit \u2014 a 46% success rate (above the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they lean run-heavy, passing <strong>46%</strong> of the time, funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Josh Jacobs</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 A Balanced Defense</h2><p>They lock down opposing WR1s \u2014 just 48 rec yds/game (vs ~58); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They surrender <strong>110 rushing</strong> and <strong>221 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>Josh Jacobs</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Jordan Love","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":9,"props":{"Comp":20.88,"Att":32.48,"Pass Yds":245.42,"Pass TD":1.79,"INT":0.65,"Rush Yds":12.22}}],"RB":[{"name":"Josh Jacobs","slot":"RB1",